### JobTrail API — try these from VS Code with the "REST Client" extension
### (click "Send Request" above each block). Backend must be running (npm run dev).

@api = http://localhost:5050/api

### Health check
GET {{api}}/health

### All applications (filters: phase=Waiting|Active|Won|Closed, q=text, sort=recent|oldest|company|priority)
GET {{api}}/applications?phase=All&sort=recent

### One application with history, calls and recruiters
GET {{api}}/applications/1

### "HR just called?" lookup (company, recruiter, email or phone digits)
GET {{api}}/lookup?q=98450

### Log a new application (one transaction: company → posting → application)
POST {{api}}/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company": "Zeta Robotics",
  "title": "Data Scientist",
  "location": "Bengaluru",
  "work_mode": "Hybrid",
  "applied_on": "2026-10-04",
  "platform": "LinkedIn Easy Apply",
  "job_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4111111111",
  "priority": 4,
  "k_name": "Ravi Kumar",
  "k_phone": "+91 90000 11111"
}

### A CHECK constraint rejects this (work_mode)
POST {{api}}/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{ "company": "X", "title": "Y", "applied_on": "2026-10-04", "work_mode": "Moon base" }

### Log an inbound HR call (trigger moves the application to SCREEN)
POST {{api}}/applications/7/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "channel": "Phone call", "direction": "Inbound", "occurred_at": "2026-10-04T11:30", "summary": "HR asked for notice period" }

### Change stage (trigger writes status_history)
PATCH {{api}}/applications/7/stage
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stage": "INTERVIEW" }

### Dashboard (reads the views)
GET {{api}}/dashboard

### Read-only SQL console
POST {{api}}/sql
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sql": "SELECT * FROM v_pipeline" }
